error[Z0406]: `quantile` needs `p:`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:3
  |
2 | w.quantile(wage)
  |   ^^^^^^^^ `p:` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `data.quantile(var, p: 0.9)` or `p: [0.25, 0.5, 0.75]`

error[Z0401]: `p:` of `quantile` must lie between 0 and 1, but this is 1.5
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:21
  |
2 | w.quantile(wage, p: 1.5)
  |                     ^^^ outside [0, 1]
  |
  = help: a quantile's probability is a share of the values: `p: 0.9` is the ninetieth percentile

error[Z0401]: `type:` of `quantile` must be one of the nine definitions, 1 to 9, not 10
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:32
  |
2 | w.quantile(wage, p: 0.5, type: 10)
  |                                ^^ not a quantile definition
  |
  = help: `type: 7` is R's default; Hyndman and Fan (1996) number the nine definitions

error[Z0401]: `p` of `quantile` must be a Float or List, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:21
  |
2 | w.quantile(wage, p: "half")
  |                     ^^^^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: usage: `data.quantile(var, p: Float | List, type: Int = 7, by: Vars, weights: Var, weight_type: frequency | analytic | sampling = sampling)`

error[Z0401]: `n()` counts the rows of a frame and stands inside `add` or `aggregate`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | n()
  | ^ no frame here
  |
  = help: write `wages.n_rows()` for a frame's row count, or `wages.add(share = x / n())` for a count inside a definition

error[Z0401]: `mean` needs a Bool, Int or Float, but `name` is Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:8
  |
2 | w.mean(name)
  |        ^^^^ a Str variable of w
  |
  = help: choose a Bool, Int or Float variable; `w.describe()` lists the types

error[Z0101]: no variable `nope` in `w`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:18
  |
2 | w.mean(wage, by: nope)
  |                  ^^^^ not a variable of w
  |
  = help: the variables of `w` are: id, wage, hours, name
